  "term": "methocarbamol",
  "definition": "Methocarbamol is a carbamate drug with centrally acting muscle-relaxant effects. Its exact action is not established, but it is thought to work through cholinesterase inhibition in the autonomic nervous system, neuromuscular junction, and central nervous system, rather than by directly acting on the muscle’s contractile machinery.",
